00:11:08.000 --> 00:12:08.000
Given the extent of Hannah and David's injuries, they believed it was a crime of passion sparked by jealousy or anger. They questioned David's travel companion Chris Ware who was highly distressed and unable to shed any light on the tragedy. Police were suspicious. Chris had an injury on his right hand which he insisted was the result of a prior accident. He said he and David had been due to leave Katow that day after the murders and they'd made no enemies during their time on the island. He couldn't think of any reason why someone would want to hurt David, who was widely adored by those who knew him. Likewise, Hannah's friends had no information that could help with the investigation. With no evidence to link Hannah or David's friends to the crime, police gave them permission to leave the island.
考虑到汉娜和大卫受伤的程度，他们认为这是一起由嫉妒或愤怒引发的激情犯罪。他们询问了大卫的旅伴克里斯·韦尔，他非常痛苦，无法为这场悲剧提供任何线索。警方表示怀疑。克里斯右手有伤，他坚称这是之前事故的结果。他说他和大卫本打算在谋杀案发生的那天离开涛岛，他们在岛上期间没有结下任何仇人。他想不出为什么有人会伤害大卫，大卫深受认识他的人的喜爱。同样，汉娜的朋友也没有任何可以帮助调查的信息。由于没有证据将汉娜或大卫的朋友与犯罪联系起来，警方允许他们离开该岛。

