这些男性的DNA也在L&M烟头上被发现，还有第三名亚洲男性的DNA。因此，韦尔兄弟被正式排除在调查之外，并获准返回英国。泰国警方现在被迫向内寻找潜在嫌疑人。汉娜和大卫最后一次露面的AC酒吧以经常有成群结队的醉酒男子出没而闻名，有人推测汉娜可能与其中一人发生了冲突，那人随后在他们走回酒店时跟踪了她和大卫。另一种可能性是渔民可能从船上游上岸实施犯罪，然后从海上逃走，而没有人知道他们在该地区。警方开始关注岛上占主导地位的缅甸移民社区。对于涛岛上约2000名常住居民来说，有大约5000名缅甸工人从邻国缅甸涌入寻找工作。由于他们愿意以比泰国人更低的工资工作，缅甸人占了岛上劳动力的绝大多数。

16
00:17:32.000 --> 00:19:00.000
Many were undocumented and often exploited and treated disrespectfully by Thais who considered them to be of a lower social standing. Burmese workers who lived or worked within the vicinity of the crime scene were rounded up en masse and required to provide DNA samples and footprints to compare to those left in the sand at the murder scene. Documentation was also checked to identify those who were working in the country illegally. Raids were done on several homes, and five Burmese men were put under the spotlight after blood stains were found on some of their clothes. All up, over 200 DNA samples were collected, but none were rematched to the crime scene. 25-year-old Scottish musician Sean McCanna had been living on Catau for some time and was a friend of David Miller's from back home. Crushed to hear what had happened, Sean deeply regretted not going to the AC bar with David on the night he was killed. In the days following the murders, he'd heard many rumours circulating around the island, including that two Thai men had attempted to molest Hannah and David had stepped in, prompting the Thais to kill the pair.
许多人没有证件，经常受到泰国人的剥削和不尊重，泰国人认为他们的社会地位较低。居住或工作在犯罪现场附近的缅甸工人被集体围捕，并被要求提供DNA样本和脚印，以与留在谋杀现场沙滩上的样本进行比对。警方还检查了证件，以确定哪些人在非法工作。几个家庭遭到突袭，五名缅甸男子因衣服上发现血迹而受到关注。总共收集了200多个DNA样本，但没有一个与犯罪现场匹配。25岁的苏格兰音乐家肖恩·麦肯纳已经在涛岛生活了一段时间，是大卫·米勒在家乡的朋友。听到发生的事情，肖恩深感悲痛，他非常后悔在大卫被杀的那晚没有和他一起去AC酒吧。在谋杀案发生后的几天里，他听到了岛上流传的许多谣言，包括两名泰国男子试图骚扰汉娜，大卫介入，导致泰国人杀害了这对情侣。

17
00:19:00.000 --> 00:20:20.000
Drowning his woes at a local bar, a group of local Thai men approached Sean and started asking him questions about his friend. Feeling tipsy, Sean answered them, before one of the men allegedly said, It was you who killed them. You've got two people's deaths on your hands. You are going to hang yourself tonight. We are going to watch you hang. You die tonight. Terrified, Sean got up and ran. He sprinted into a nearby supermarket, but two of the men followed him inside. Thinking quickly about how to protect himself, Sean logged into Facebook on his phone and posted a photo of the men along with the message, Thai mafia are trying to kill me. Please help me. The police eventually escorted Sean back to his hotel, but fearing for his life, he fled into the jungle where he hid overnight, before boarding the first boat off Katow in the morning. He then met up with the reporter for the Daily Telegraph to tell his story, saying he believed the men who approached him knew who had killed Hannah and David and were looking for a scapegoat.
在当地一家酒吧借酒消愁时，一群当地泰国男子走近肖恩，开始问他关于他朋友的问题。喝醉了的肖恩回答了他们，随后其中一名男子据称说：“是你杀了他们。你背负着两条人命。你今晚会自杀的。我们会看着你上吊。你今晚就得死。”惊恐万分的肖恩起身逃跑。他冲进附近的一家超市，但其中两名男子跟着他进去了。肖恩迅速思考如何保护自己，他在手机上登录Facebook，发布了一张这些男人的照片，并附上信息：“泰国黑手党想杀我。请帮帮我。”警察最终护送肖恩回到酒店，但由于担心自己的生命安全，他逃进了丛林，在那里躲了一夜，然后在早上登上了离开涛岛的第一艘船。他随后会见了《每日电讯报》的一名记者讲述了他的故事，说他相信那些接近他的男人知道是谁杀了汉娜和大卫，并且正在寻找替罪羊。

18
00:20:20.000 --> 00:21:51.000
They wanted Sean to take his own life, so that it would fit with their narrative that the killer was a Westerner. When the video of Sean talking about this encounter circulated online, some astute viewers noticed that he had a 2cm long wound on his right forearm that looked remarkably similar to one on David Miller's shoulder. Photos also circulated on social media of Sean's guitar, which he had left on Katow, and it appeared to be splattered with blood. Suspicions arose that Sean could have been involved in the murders, possibly in conjunction with some of his Thai friends, and had created the story about being threatened in order to detract attention from himself. Sean strongly disputed these allegations, explaining that the injuries and blood had come from a bike accident days before the murders. He left the country and went off the grid. Unlike other parts of the world, in Thailand the term mafia doesn't necessarily relate to organised crime, but to the influential families that hold a monopoly over certain areas. Katow initially served as a political prison, with its first permanent inhabitants arriving in the 1930s, long before any authorities.
他们想让肖恩自杀，这样就符合他们关于凶手是西方人的说法。当肖恩谈论这次遭遇的视频在网上流传时，一些敏锐的观众注意到他的右前臂上有一道2厘米长的伤口，看起来和大卫·米勒肩膀上的伤口惊人地相似。肖恩留在涛岛的吉他的照片也在社交媒体上流传，上面似乎溅满了血迹。人们开始怀疑肖恩可能参与了谋杀案，可能与他的一些泰国朋友串通，并编造了被威胁的故事以转移对自己的注意力。肖恩强烈反驳了这些指控，解释说伤口和血迹来自谋杀案发生前几天的自行车事故。他离开了这个国家并隐姓埋名。与世界其他地方不同，在泰国，“黑手党”一词并不一定指有组织犯罪，而是指在某些地区拥有垄断地位的有影响力家族。涛岛最初被用作政治监狱，其第一批常住居民在20世纪30年代到达，远在任何当局之前。

19
00:21:51.000 --> 00:23:16.000
While Katow had since been resettled into a tourist haven, these families still dominated the island, owning a majority of the land and businesses. They held great power and were generally considered the unofficial leaders of the island, the go-to people when any problems arose. The richest and most influential family on Katow was the Doh Wichien family. Feared by many, they owned a majority of the businesses on Siree Beach, including the AC bar and resort where David and Hannah were last seen alive. At the head of the family was Warapan Doh Wichien, followed closely by his brother Mondri Wat, better known as Mon. Mon had been the first person to arrive at the crime scene after the beach cleaner alerted him to the discovery of the bodies. When footage from the scene was broadcast on the news, it struck many as odd that Mon was allowed to join the police in the cordoned off area. He was seen freely walking around the crime scene, which skeptics believe gave him the opportunity to contaminate any evidence while providing a valid explanation as to why any of his DNA might be found.
虽然涛岛后来被重新安置为一个旅游天堂，但这些家族仍然统治着该岛，拥有大部分土地和企业。他们拥有巨大的权力，通常被认为是岛上的非官方领导人，是出现任何问题时的首选人物。涛岛上最富有、最有影响力的家族是Doh Wichien家族。许多人对他们感到恐惧，他们拥有塞里海滩上的大部分企业，包括大卫和汉娜最后一次活着露面的AC酒吧和度假村。家族首领是Warapan Doh Wichien，紧随其后的是他的兄弟Mondri Wat，也就是众所周知的Mon。Mon是海滩清洁工提醒他发现尸体后第一个到达犯罪现场的人。当现场录像在新闻中播出时，许多人觉得Mon被允许加入警察在警戒线内感到奇怪。他被看到在犯罪现场自由走动，怀疑论者认为这让他有机会污染任何证据，同时为为什么可能发现他的任何DNA提供了合理的解释。

20
00:23:16.000 --> 00:24:54.000
Suspicions immediately arose that the Thai mafia were involved in the murders and were working in conjunction with the police to make the problem go away. Some Thai police had a reputation for corruption and were often accused of accepting bribes and protecting those in positions of power. Bolstering these theories was the fact that Mon Doh Wichien was one of the men that Sean McKenna had photographed after they followed him into the supermarket urging him to take his own life. The other was a police officer. As accusations of a cover-up gathered momentum, the police announced they wouldn't be swayed by any local influence and that the mafia would be looked into like anyone else. Just over a week after the double homicide, police announced that Mon Doh Wichien had been taken into custody for questioning after he was captured in CCTV footage in the vicinity of the crime scene around the time the murders took place. They also sought to arrest Mon's nephew, 22-year-old Noomsad Doh Wichien, who bore resemblance to another figure captured in the footage and was reported to have fled the island shortly after the murders. Rumors swelled that Noomsad had hired a speedboat in the early hours of September 15 and was seen speeding towards the mainland, leaving his family to cover for him.
人们立即怀疑泰国黑手党参与了谋杀案，并与警方合作以消除这个问题。一些泰国警察有腐败的名声，经常被指控接受贿赂并保护那些掌权的人。支持这些理论的事实是，Mon Doh Wichien是肖恩·麦肯纳在他们跟踪他进入超市并敦促他自杀后拍摄的男子之一。另一个人是一名警察。随着掩盖真相的指控愈演愈烈，警方宣布他们不会受到任何地方势力的影响，黑手党会像其他人一样受到调查。双重谋杀案发生一周多后，警方宣布Mon Doh Wichien已被拘留审问，因为他在谋杀案发生时被闭路电视录像拍到在犯罪现场附近。他们还试图逮捕Mon的侄子，22岁的Noomsad Doh Wichien，他与录像中拍到的另一个人长相相似，据报道在谋杀案发生后不久就逃离了该岛。谣言四起，称Noomsad在9月15日凌晨租了一艘快艇，被看到向大陆疾驰而去，留下他的家人为他掩护。

21
00:24:54.000 --> 00:26:26.000
Noomsad was eventually located, but he claimed he hadn't been on Katao at the time of the murders at all. He said he'd been over 400km away at university in Bangkok and even had stills taken from CCTV footage to prove it. Concluding this to be a solid alibi, Noomsad was publicly cleared from the investigation, as was his uncle Mon. Mon later explained on the Channel 4 documentary Murder in Paradise that the real reason he chased Sean McKenna into the supermarket was because he wanted to question him about the blood on his guitar. By now, online sleuths had become fixated on the case and they remained convinced that the mafia were involved in Hannah and David's murders. Examining the CCTV stills of Noomsad Doichien in Bangkok, they noticed that the footage hadn't come from the university at all, but from the lobby of Noomsad's Bangkok apartment next door. It was time stamped at 9.15am on September 15, several hours after the murders were thought to have taken place. Some online sleuths speculated that the look of the lobby was outdated, indicating the footage had been captured some time ago, but there was no evidence to support this.
Noomsad最终被找到，但他声称在谋杀案发生时他根本不在涛岛。他说他在400多公里外的曼谷上大学，甚至有从闭路电视录像中截取的剧照来证明这一点。结论是这是一个可靠的不在场证明，Noomsad被公开排除在调查之外，他的叔叔Mon也被排除。Mon后来在第四频道纪录片《天堂谋杀案》中解释说，他追赶肖恩·麦肯纳进入超市的真正原因是想询问他关于吉他上血迹的事。到目前为止，网络侦探已经沉迷于此案，他们仍然确信黑手党参与了汉娜和大卫的谋杀案。检查Noomsad Doichien在曼谷的闭路电视剧照时，他们注意到录像根本不是来自大学，而是来自隔壁Noomsad曼谷公寓的大堂。时间戳是9月15日上午9点15分，在谋杀案被认为发生后的几个小时。一些网络侦探推测大堂的样子已经过时，表明录像是在很久以前拍摄的，但没有证据支持这一点。

22
00:26:26.000 --> 00:27:41.000
Allegations arose that the stills were fake and concerned citizens called for CCTV footage from the university itself to be released. Regardless, police closed the book on the Doichien family. Frustrated by the accusations against his family, Katow Hedman, Warapan Doichien announced the bizarre challenge. If anyone could prove that his family were involved in Hannah and David's murders, he'd pay them 1 million baht, the equivalent to around 40,000 Australian dollars. Two weeks passed without any significant breakthroughs in the case. The police came under criticism from the British press for chasing the wrong leads, publicly naming suspects who were later cleared and for wrongly jumping from one suspect to the next without fully completing each line of inquiry. Thai police rejected an offer of assistance from the British Embassy, saying they were confident that an arrest would soon be made. One BBC journalist remarked,
有指控称这些剧照是伪造的，有关公民呼吁发布大学本身的闭路电视录像。无论如何，警方结案了Doichien家族的调查。涛岛头目Warapan Doichien对针对他家族的指控感到沮丧，宣布了一个奇怪的挑战。如果有人能证明他的家族参与了汉娜和大卫的谋杀案，他将支付他们100万泰铢，相当于约4万澳元。两周过去了，案件没有任何重大突破。警方因追查错误线索、公开点名后来被洗清嫌疑的嫌疑人以及在没有完全完成每条调查线索的情况下错误地从一个嫌疑人跳到另一个嫌疑人而受到英国媒体的批评。泰国警方拒绝了英国大使馆的协助提议，称他们有信心很快就会逮捕凶手。一位BBC记者评论道：

23
00:27:41.000 --> 00:29:14.000
Watching the Thai police struggle to answer this mystery with the eyes of the world on them has felt like being part of a sometimes farcical performance in which we, the media, are the audience. There were roughly 300 CCTV cameras around Siree Beach, but only 106 of them were working on the night that Hannah Witheridge and David Miller were killed. Security cameras at the AC bar didn't face towards the beachside exit, so it couldn't be determined exactly when Hannah and David had left the venue. Given that David had entered around 208am and the pair's bodies had been found around 5am, the murders had occurred somewhere within that time frame. CCTV footage captured in the area within those hours revealed three young Asian males travelling on a motorcycle with a guitar in tow. After stopping at a 7-11 convenience store to buy beer and cigarettes, the trio made their way towards the beach and disappeared from view. Later, at around 3.45am, a security camera at a health restaurant near the crime scene captured an Asian man running shirtless down the street. Although he soon disappeared from view, his shadow could be seen entering a shortcut that led to a nearby bungalow.
“看着泰国警方在全世界的注视下努力回答这个谜团，感觉就像是在参与一场有时是闹剧的表演，而我们媒体就是观众。”塞里海滩周围大约有300个闭路电视摄像头，但在汉娜·威瑟里奇和大卫·米勒被杀的那晚，只有106个在工作。AC酒吧的监控摄像头没有对着海滩出口，因此无法确定汉娜和大卫确切离开该场所的时间。考虑到大卫在凌晨2点08分左右进入，而两人的尸体在凌晨5点左右被发现，谋杀案发生在那个时间段内的某个地方。在该时间段内拍摄的闭路电视录像显示，三名年轻的亚洲男性骑着摩托车，带着一把吉他。在7-11便利店停下来买啤酒和香烟后，三人朝海滩走去，消失在视野中。后来，在凌晨3点45分左右，犯罪现场附近一家健康餐厅的监控摄像头拍到一名亚洲男子赤裸上身在街上奔跑。虽然他很快消失在视野中，但可以看到他的影子进入了一条通往附近平房的捷径。

24
00:29:14.000 --> 00:30:35.000
On October 1, just over two weeks after the murders, police visited the bungalow and found that a young Burmese migrant named Mormor resided there. When asked about his whereabouts on the night of the murders, Mormor said he had gone down to Surrey Beach with two of his friends, Zor-Lyn and Waypo, to play the guitar. They'd sat on a fallen log underneath a pine tree sharing cigarettes and having a few drinks. Mormor then rode the motorcycle to his girlfriend's house. When he returned home, Zor-Lyn and Waypo were there asleep. He didn't notice anything out of the ordinary nor was there anything strange about their behaviour in the days following. Police ordered Mormor to take them to the homes of Zor-Lyn and Waypo for further questioning. At 1am on October 2, a team of police swarmed the house where the men lived with six other workers. 22-year-old Zor-Lyn had grown up poor and uneducated in a remote village in Myanmar's Rakhine state that had no electricity or running water.
10月1日，即谋杀案发生两周多后，警方走访了该平房，发现一名叫Mormor的年轻缅甸移民住在那里。当被问及谋杀案当晚的行踪时，Mormor说他和两个朋友Zor-Lyn和Waypo去了塞里海滩弹吉他。他们坐在松树下的一根倒下的原木上，分享香烟并喝了几杯酒。Mormor随后骑摩托车去了他女朋友家。当他回到家时，Zor-Lyn和Waypo在那里睡觉。他没有注意到任何异常，在接下来的几天里他们的行为也没有什么奇怪的地方。警方命令Mormor带他们去Zor-Lyn和Waypo的住处进行进一步询问。10月2日凌晨1点，一队警察包围了这些人与另外六名工人居住的房子。22岁的Zor-Lyn在缅甸若开邦的一个偏远村庄长大，那里贫穷且没有受过教育，没有电也没有自来水。

25
00:30:35.000 --> 00:31:57.000
His family grew just enough crops and raised just enough livestock to get by. After his father passed away, Zor-Lyn crossed the border into Thailand looking for better paying work and secured a job at a bar on Surrey Beach. Although it didn't pay well, it was more than he could make in Myanmar and he worked hard to send as much money as he could to his mother back home. Police asked to see Zor-Lyn's passport but he couldn't provide one so they placed him under arrest for illegally entering the country. As for 22-year-old Waypo, he was nowhere to be found. Like a Zor-Lyn, Waypo also came from a poor remote village in Myanmar's Rakhine state with very limited resources and had come to Khatau to take advantage of the employment opportunities. He'd recently been offered a new job on the mainland and was currently travelling on an overnight boat that was due to arrive in the city of Surat Tani at 6am. When the boat pulled in, officers found Waypo hiding on board and placed him under arrest when he was unable to provide a passport or valid work permit.
他的家人种的庄稼和养的牲畜刚好够维持生计。父亲去世后，Zor-Lyn越过边境进入泰国寻找报酬更高的工作，并在塞里海滩的一家酒吧找到了一份工作。虽然工资不高，但比他在缅甸能赚到的多，他努力工作，尽可能多地寄钱给家乡的母亲。警方要求查看Zor-Lyn的护照，但他无法提供，因此他们以非法入境为由将他逮捕。至于22岁的Waypo，他不知去向。像Zor-Lyn一样，Waypo也来自缅甸若开邦一个贫穷偏远的村庄，资源非常有限，来到涛岛是为了利用就业机会。他最近在大陆得到了一份新工作，目前正乘坐一艘通宵船，预计于凌晨6点到达素叻他尼市。当船靠岸时，警察发现Waypo躲在船上，在他无法提供护照或有效工作许可证时将他逮捕。

26
00:31:57.000 --> 00:33:11.000
In custody, they were questioned as potential witnesses to the murder of Hannah and David. Both men signed written forms consenting to have their DNA collected. Waypo was taken back to Khatau for questioning and it didn't take long for him to crack. Within hours, Waypo confessed to everything. In Thailand, it is customary for those accused of committing major crimes to participate in a public re-enactment of their offences. The purpose is to help investigators visualise the crimes and to corroborate confessions, but it also serves as a form of public humiliation. Thai culture places a large emphasis on what's known as face, which is similar to the western concept of reputation. Losing face is something that Thai people avoid at all costs and a public re-enactment of one's crimes serves as the ultimate degradation.
在拘留期间，他们作为汉娜和大卫谋杀案的潜在证人受到审问。两人都签署了书面表格，同意采集DNA。Waypo被带回涛岛接受审问，没过多久他就崩溃了。几个小时内，Waypo承认了一切。在泰国，被指控犯有重大罪行的人通常会参加犯罪现场的公开重演。目的是帮助调查人员直观地了解犯罪过程并证实供词，但它也起到了一种公开羞辱的形式。泰国文化非常强调所谓的“面子”，这类似于西方的声誉概念。丢脸是泰国人极力避免的事情，公开重演自己的罪行是终极的贬低。

27
00:33:11.000 --> 00:34:29.000
On October 3, hordes of press and curious onlookers gathered around a siree beach as Xorlin and Waypo were led to the crime scene in handcuffs. Wearing bulletproof vests and helmets for their own protection, the two men used a dustpan in place of the garden hoe. As instructed by the police, Xorlin and Waypo re-enacted their movements from the early hours of the morning on September 15, complete with the guitar. According to the official police report, it all started after their friend Momo left to visit his girlfriend. Xorlin and Waypo remained sitting on a fallen log playing the guitar and smoking cigarettes when through the darkness they saw Hannah and David kissing. In a conservative country where public affection is frowned upon and rarely seen, the sire aroused them. Overcome with sexual jealousy, they decided to knock David out so that they could rape Hannah. The pair found the garden hoe nearby and snuck up behind the couple, striking David on the head several times.
10月3日，大批媒体和好奇的旁观者聚集在塞里海滩，Xorlin和Waypo被戴上手铐带到犯罪现场。为了自身安全，两人穿着防弹背心和头盔，用簸箕代替了锄头。按照警方的指示，Xorlin和Waypo重演了他们9月15日清晨的动作，并带上了吉他。根据官方警方报告，这一切始于他们的朋友Momo离开去见女朋友之后。Xorlin和Waypo坐在倒下的原木上弹吉他、抽烟，这时他们在黑暗中看到汉娜和大卫在接吻。在一个保守的国家，公开亲热是不被赞成的，也很少见到，这种景象激怒了他们。出于性嫉妒，他们决定打晕大卫，以便强奸汉娜。两人在附近找到了锄头，悄悄溜到这对情侣身后，多次击打大卫的头部。

28
00:34:29.000 --> 00:35:33.000
Realising he was dead, they dragged his body into the sea. They then used the hoe to inflict several blows to Hannah's head, rendering her unconscious, at which point they took turns raping her. Afterwards, they knew they had to kill Hannah to conceal what they'd done, so they hit her in the head with the hoe several more times. Waypo then stole David's sunglasses and iPhone. He broke the sunglasses and threw them away, but gave the iPhone to a friend named Ren. Officers went to Ren's home and found the smashed broken iPhone in the backyard. A check of its serial number with British authorities confirmed that it belonged to David Miller. Armed with the confession, the authorities were able to place a rush on the DNA testing, and it was soon revealed that the semen on Hannah's body had come from both Zorlin and Waypo.
意识到他已经死了，他们把他的尸体拖进海里。然后他们用锄头多次击打汉娜的头部，使她失去知觉，此时他们轮流强奸了她。事后，他们知道必须杀死汉娜以掩盖他们的所作所为，所以他们又用锄头击打了她的头部几次。Waypo随后偷走了大卫的太阳镜和iPhone。他弄坏了太阳镜并扔掉了，但把iPhone给了朋友Ren。警察去了Ren的家，在后院发现了被砸碎的iPhone。与英国当局核对序列号后，证实它属于大卫·米勒。有了供词，当局得以加快DNA检测速度，很快发现汉娜尸体上的精液来自Zorlin和Waypo两人。

29
00:35:33.000 --> 00:37:06.000
Their DNA was also found on the murder weapon and on cigarette butts recovered from the crime scene. Zorlin and Waypo were both formally charged with five offences, premeditated murder, killing to conceal a criminal offence, rape, illegal entry into Thailand, and staying in the country without permission. Many members of the public had believed it was just a matter of time before the crimes were blamed on a migrant, and when news hit that the Burmese workers had been arrested for the murders, skepticism ran rife. A commentary in the Bangkok Post explained that the skepticism didn't just stem from the poor handling of the police investigation, but quote, from the police's longstanding notoriety for arresting poor and powerless scapegoats to save rich criminals who can afford to buy their innocence. The public outrage became so strong that police threatened to charge anyone who questioned their findings. The National Police Chief described the investigation as a perfect job, but for the critics, there were several details about Zorlin and Waypo's alleged involvement that raised serious questions. First of all, when the two men were taken into police custody, they were only questioned as witnesses, not suspects.
他们的DNA也在凶器和从犯罪现场回收的烟头上被发现。Zorlin和Waypo都被正式指控犯有五项罪行：蓄意谋杀、杀人以掩盖犯罪、强奸、非法进入泰国以及未经许可在境内停留。许多公众认为将罪行归咎于移民只是时间问题，当缅甸工人因谋杀案被捕的消息传出时，怀疑论盛行。《曼谷邮报》的一篇评论解释说，这种怀疑不仅源于警方调查处理不当，而且“源于警方长期以来因逮捕贫穷无力的替罪羊以拯救有钱购买清白的罪犯而臭名昭著”。公众的愤怒变得如此强烈，以至于警方威胁要起诉任何质疑他们调查结果的人。国家警察局长将这次调查描述为“完美的工作”，但对于批评者来说，关于Zorlin和Waypo涉案的几个细节引发了严重的问题。首先，当这两名男子被警方拘留时，他们只是作为证人而不是嫌疑人受到审问。

30
00:37:06.000 --> 00:39:02.000
It was therefore suspicious that they would both voluntarily confess to such serious crimes in the absence of any incriminating evidence. There was talk that the police might have offered the two Burmese men money in exchange for a confession, which they ignorantly agreed to without realizing the seriousness of the consequences. During the re-enactment of the murders, some noted that Zorlin and Waypo had to be guided every step of the way, as though they had no idea what was expected of them. As described by author Suzanne Buchanan in her book titled The Curse of the Turtle, the true story of Thailand's backpacker murders, the accused were often manhandled into position by the police, and if they pointed in one direction, the police would correct them and they'd then point the opposite way. Suzanne remarked, Zorlin and Waypo visibly had no clue what they were meant to be doing. They had to be physically prompted at every turn by the police who were obviously choreographing the entire thing. The two tiny men looked like puppets on a string. Critics also questioned Zorlin and Waypo's supposed motive. When announcing the arrests, police initially said that the killers had been aroused upon seeing Hannah and David, quote, making love, but this explanation didn't add up. For one, David's DNA wasn't found on Hannah's body, meaning the pair hadn't had sex. Secondly, to say that the killers had been spontaneously motivated by sexual desire contrasted scientific studies about what drives men to rape women.
因此，在没有任何确凿证据的情况下，他们两人会自愿承认如此严重的罪行，这本身就很可疑。有传言称，警方可能曾向这两名缅甸男子提供金钱以换取供词，而他们因无知而同意了，却没意识到后果的严重性。在谋杀案现场重演过程中，一些人注意到，佐林和怀波每一步都需要被引导，仿佛他们根本不知道别人期望他们做什么。正如作家苏珊·布坎南在她的书《海龟的诅咒：泰国背包客谋杀案的真实故事》中所述，被告经常被警察粗暴地摆布到指定位置，如果他们指向一个方向，警察会纠正他们，然后他们就会指向相反的方向。苏珊评论道，佐林和怀波显然根本不知道他们应该做什么。他们每走一步都必须由显然在编排整个过程的警察进行身体上的提示。这两个瘦小的男人看起来就像提线木偶。批评人士还质疑了佐林和怀波所谓的动机。在宣布逮捕时，警方最初称凶手在看到汉娜和戴维“做爱”时产生了性冲动，但这种解释根本站不住脚。首先，戴维的DNA并没有在汉娜的尸体上发现，这意味着两人并没有发生性关系。其次，说凶手是受性欲自发驱动的，这与关于男性强奸女性动机的科学研究相矛盾。

31
00:39:02.000 --> 00:40:35.000
A majority of psychologists believe that rape isn't driven by lust, but is usually an act of premeditated violence driven by the desire for power and control. For some, the police misunderstanding served as further proof that they were creating a narrative against the two accused in the absence of any real motive. There was also the question of whether Zorlin and Waypo were physically capable of overpowering two victims. Both of the Burmese men were very slight in stature, only standing around five foot tall, whereas David Miller was roughly six foot two with an athletic build. Striking David in the head, overpowering him and dragging his body into the water while simultaneously restraining Hannah would have been no easy feat for two men of the accused's size. Furthermore, 20 days had passed between the murders taking place and Zorlin and Waypo being arrested, yet the pair had made no attempt to flee the island. Reports stated that Waypo was arrested when trying to escape on a boat to Surat Tani, but Waypo claimed he'd simply been visiting the mainland to start a new job. If the two Burmese migrants were responsible for the murders, it made sense that they would have left the island as soon as possible to escape not just the authorities, but also the local mafia.
大多数心理学家认为，强奸并非由欲望驱动，通常是一种由权力和控制欲驱动的预谋暴力行为。对一些人来说，警方的误解进一步证明了他们在没有任何真实动机的情况下，编造了针对两名被告的叙事。还有一个问题是，佐林和怀波是否有能力制服两名受害者。这两名缅甸男子身材都非常瘦小，身高只有五英尺左右，而戴维·米勒身高约六英尺二英寸，体格健壮。对于两个被告这样体型的人来说，要击中戴维的头部、制服他并将他的尸体拖入水中，同时还要控制住汉娜，绝非易事。此外，从谋杀发生到佐林和怀波被捕已经过去了20天，但两人并没有试图逃离该岛。有报道称，怀波在试图乘船逃往素叻他尼时被捕，但怀波声称他只是去大陆找一份新工作。如果这两名缅甸移民是谋杀案的凶手，那么他们理应尽快离开该岛，以逃避不仅是当局，还有当地黑帮的追捕。

32
00:40:35.000 --> 00:41:58.000
These details aside, some were also suspicious about the police handling of the evidence. David's body and clothing belonging to both him and Hannah had been moved shortly after officers first arrived at the crime scene, potentially disturbing evidence. Police explained they did this to avoid the items being washed away by the tide, but the tide had already gone out for the day and it was therefore unlikely that the items would be dragged away by the current. Human rights groups had been following Hannah and David's case and were concerned that Zorlin and Waypo had been treated unfairly. From the get-go, it was clear that police didn't want the killer to be tied. Not only had one of the lead investigators said there was no way a Thai person could be capable of such a crime, the sub-district head of Katau commented, If another foreigner killed Hannah and David, then the damage for us won't be too bad. If it's something else, it could really hurt our reputation. When Zorlin and Waypo were arrested, the DNA consent forms and statements they signed were both written in Thai.
撇开这些细节不谈，一些人还对警方处理证据的方式表示怀疑。在警察首次到达犯罪现场后不久，戴维的尸体以及属于他和汉娜的衣物就被移动了，这可能破坏了证据。警方解释说，他们这样做是为了防止物品被潮水冲走，但当时潮水已经退去，因此这些物品不太可能被水流冲走。人权组织一直在关注汉娜和戴维的案件，并担心佐林和怀波受到了不公正的对待。从一开始，就很明显警方不想让真正的凶手被抓获。不仅其中一名首席调查员曾说泰国人不可能犯下这样的罪行，卡陶的副区长还评论道：“如果另一个外国人杀了汉娜和戴维，对我们来说损失不会太大。如果是其他情况，可能会严重损害我们的声誉。”当佐林和怀波被捕时，他们签署的DNA同意书和声明都是用泰语书写的。

33
00:41:58.000 --> 00:43:18.000
However, neither of the Burmese men could speak or read Thai. They'd been provided with a Burmese translator, but he wasn't an official court-appointed translator. He was a Burmese pancake vendor who spoke neither Thai, nor Zorlin and Waypo's native Rakhine dialect. The pancake vendor was also part of an ethnic minority that had a long history of conflict with Myanmar's Rakhine state, which is where Zorlin and Waypo came from. There were also concerns that the public re-enactment, which human rights groups viewed as antiquated, would harm the accused's right to a fair trial. Officials from the Myanmar Embassy visited Zorlin and Waypo in jail, along with members of Thailand's National Human Rights Commission, the Lawyers' Council of Thailand, and the Migrant Workers' Rights Network. They determined that both men were naive, uneducated, and easily coerced. Along with the forced DNA testing and questionable translator, the accused hadn't been appointed a lawyer or told of their rights.
然而，这两名缅甸男子都不会说也不会读泰语。他们虽然被提供了一名缅甸语翻译，但他并不是法院指定的官方翻译。他是一名缅甸煎饼小贩，既不会说泰语，也不会说佐林和怀波的母语若开语。这名煎饼小贩还属于一个与缅甸若开邦（佐林和怀波的家乡）有着长期冲突历史的少数民族。人们还担心，人权组织认为过时的公开重演会损害被告获得公平审判的权利。缅甸大使馆的官员与泰国国家人权委员会、泰国律师协会和移民工人权利网络的成员一起在监狱中探望了佐林和怀波。他们认定这两名男子天真、未受过教育，且容易受到胁迫。除了强制性的DNA检测和有问题的翻译外，被告也没有被指派律师，也没有被告知他们的权利。

34
00:43:18.000 --> 00:44:34.000
They didn't seem to understand the full weight of the crimes they'd been accused of, nor the fact that they wouldn't be released anytime soon. Another detail that couldn't be overlooked was the fact that the two young men appeared to be sporting several bruises. Zorlin and Waypo told these organisations that what really happened on the night of the murders was that they'd met at Mormor's workplace, which was part of a resort owned by the Dorwichian family. They waited around for Mormor to finish, and the trio then purchased some beer and cigarettes from a 7-Eleven before riding a motorbike down to Syri Beach. At around 2am, they sat on a fallen log playing a guitar that Zorlin had brought with him. It was dark, and they couldn't see more than roughly 5 metres in front of them. They spent roughly an hour playing the guitar while passing the beers and cigarettes between them. Mormor then left for a while, at which point Zorlin and Waypo made another quick trip to the convenience store to buy two more bottles of beer.
他们似乎并不了解自己所受指控的严重性，也不明白他们不会很快被释放。另一个不容忽视的细节是，这两名年轻人身上似乎有多处淤青。佐林和怀波告诉这些组织，谋杀案当晚真正发生的事情是，他们在莫莫的工作场所见面，那是多维奇安家族拥有的一个度假村的一部分。他们等莫莫下班，然后三人从7-Eleven便利店买了一些啤酒和香烟，骑摩托车去了叙利亚海滩。凌晨2点左右，他们坐在倒下的原木上，弹奏着佐林带来的吉他。天很黑，他们看不清前方大约5米以外的东西。他们花了大约一个小时弹吉他，同时轮流喝啤酒和抽烟。莫莫随后离开了一会儿，这时佐林和怀波又快速去便利店买了另外两瓶啤酒。

35
00:44:34.000 --> 00:45:41.000
Shortly after they returned to the beach, Mormor rejoined them, but he didn't stay long before heading off to visit his girlfriend. It started to lightly rain, so Zorlin and Waypo decided to call it a night. As they made their way along the beach, Zorlin decided to take a quick dip in the sea in the hopes of curbing a nagging headache. He placed the guitar down and jumped into the water fully clothed. Waypo decided to join him, taking off his shoes and shirt and piling them onto the shore. They swam for around 15 minutes, and when they got out, Waypo's shoes, shirt and the guitar were missing. There was a group of about 20 people watching a fire-twirling show outside the AC bar, but other than that, they hadn't seen anyone pass by. At no point did they see Hannah Witheridge or David Miller.
他们回到海滩后不久，莫莫就加入了他们，但他没待多久就去见他的女朋友了。天开始下起小雨，所以佐林和怀波决定结束这一晚。当他们沿着海滩走时，佐林决定去海里快速游个泳，希望能缓解恼人的头痛。他放下吉他，穿着衣服跳进了水里。怀波决定加入他，脱掉鞋子和衬衫，堆在岸上。他们游了大约15分钟，当他们出来时，怀波的鞋子、衬衫和吉他都不见了。有一群大约20人在AC酒吧外看火舞表演，除此之外，他们没有看到任何人经过。他们自始至终都没有看到汉娜·威瑟里奇或戴维·米勒。

36
00:45:41.000 --> 00:46:51.000
The two men walked around looking for their belongings but couldn't find them, so they decided to make the short walk back to Mormor's bungalow, taking a shortcut down a nearby laneway. Mormor was still at his girlfriend's house, so Zorlin and Waypo let themselves inside. Zorlin hung his wet clothes out to dry and went to bed, but Waypo couldn't relax. The missing shirt he'd been wearing belonged to Mormor, and he wanted to return it, plus he needed his shoes for work the next day. Waypo returned to the beach on his own, but still couldn't find the missing items. Admitting defeat, he walked back to Mormor's house, finding an iPhone and pair of sunglasses along the way, which he decided to keep. He got back to Mormor's bungalow around 4am, with Mormor returning from his girlfriend's shortly after. The next morning, Zorlin and Waypo returned to the village where they both lived.
两人四处寻找他们的财物，但没找到，于是他们决定步行回到莫莫的平房，抄近路走过附近的一条小巷。莫莫还在他女朋友家，所以佐林和怀波自己进去了。佐林把湿衣服挂起来晾干并上床睡觉，但怀波无法放松。他穿的那件丢失的衬衫是莫莫的，他想还回去，而且他第二天工作还需要鞋子。怀波独自回到海滩，但仍然找不到丢失的物品。承认失败后，他走回莫莫的房子，途中发现了一部iPhone和一副太阳镜，他决定留着。他在凌晨4点左右回到莫莫的平房，莫莫不久后也从他女朋友那里回来了。第二天早上，佐林和怀波回到了他们居住的村庄。

37
00:46:51.000 --> 00:48:12.000
Waypo showed the iPhone to his friend Ren. Waypo tried to turn the phone on, but it required a passcode, so he plugged it into Ren's charger and left it there before heading off for work. When Ren later heard about Hannah and David's murders, he panicked. Realising that Waypo had found the iPhone right near the crime scene, Ren smashed the phone to pieces and hid it behind his house, out of fear that he'd be implicated in the crime. The two accused claimed this was the same version of events that they'd given when they were first taken in for questioning, but the police didn't believe them. Instead, they'd taken DNA samples without Zorlin and Waypo's consent and forced them to sign documents written in Thai which they didn't understand. When Zorlin denied committing the murders, the Burmese translator attacked him, threatening that he'd be killed and thrown to sea. The translator urged him to confess, saying that he'd only get four or five years in prison as opposed to certain death.
怀波把iPhone给他的朋友任看。怀波试图打开手机，但需要密码，所以他把它插在任的充电器上，然后就去上班了。当任后来听说汉娜和戴维被谋杀的消息时，他惊慌失措。意识到怀波在犯罪现场附近发现了iPhone，任出于害怕自己会被牵连进这起罪行，把手机砸得粉碎并藏在他家后面。两名被告声称，这就是他们第一次被带去审讯时给出的版本，但警察不相信他们。相反，他们在未经佐林和怀波同意的情况下提取了DNA样本，并强迫他们签署了他们看不懂的泰文文件。当佐林否认犯下谋杀罪时，缅甸翻译攻击了他，威胁说他会被杀并扔进海里。翻译敦促他认罪，说他只会坐牢四五年，而不是必死无疑。

38
00:48:12.000 --> 00:49:08.000
Both men claimed that police tortured them by stripping them naked and leaving them in heavily air-conditioned rooms with blindfolds and handcuffs on. A plastic bag was placed over Zorlin's head in an attempt to suffocate him. Waypo was beaten and had his testicles electrocuted. At one point, the police allegedly said that other Burmese workers had been burnt to death on the island and warned. Those who don't have passports don't have rights. If they disappear, nobody would notice. Humiliated, terrified and in agony, Zorlin and Waypo eventually couldn't take it anymore. Both men reluctantly confessed to the crime. At no point were they informed of the charges against them or of their rights to a lawyer.
两人都声称警察通过剥光他们的衣服，把他们关在空调开得很足的房间里，并蒙住眼睛和戴上手铐来折磨他们。一个塑料袋被套在佐林的头上，试图让他窒息。怀波遭到殴打，睾丸受到电击。有一次，警察据称说岛上还有其他缅甸工人被活活烧死，并警告说：“没有护照的人就没有权利。如果他们消失了，没人会注意到。”佐林和怀波感到羞辱、恐惧和痛苦，最终无法再忍受了。两人不情愿地承认了罪行。他们自始至终都没有被告知对他们的指控，也没有被告知他们聘请律师的权利。

39
00:49:08.000 --> 00:50:47.000
When Zorlin and Waypo were whisked off to Siree Beach to stage a re-enactment the next day, they claimed the Burmese translator dictated their every move, instructing them what to do and say. A legal team from the Lawyers' Council of Thailand agreed to take on the case pro bono and almost two months after Hannah and David's murders, Zorlin and Waypo formally retracted their earlier statements and both declared that they'd be pleading not guilty to the crime. Myanmar officials warned that unfair treatment of Zorlin and Waypo could harm the relationship between the two countries, but Thai police staunchly denied the allegations of torture. They maintained that their interrogations had been done by the book and both of the accused had confessed at their own volition. The public prosecutor stated that the retracted confessions wouldn't have any impact on the case due to the strength of the forensic evidence. The families of Hannah Witheridge and David Miller slammed the reports that Zorlin and Waypo had been used as scapegoats and expressed confidence in the investigation. The Millers said, From what we have seen, the suspects have a difficult case to answer. The evidence against them appears to be powerful and convincing.
当佐林和怀波第二天被匆匆带到西里海滩进行现场重演时，他们声称缅甸翻译指挥了他们的一举一动，指示他们做什么和说什么。泰国律师协会的一个法律团队同意无偿接手此案，在汉娜和戴维被谋杀近两个月后，佐林和怀波正式撤回了他们之前的陈述，并都宣布他们将对该罪行进行无罪抗辩。缅甸官员警告说，对佐林和怀波的不公正待遇可能会损害两国之间的关系，但泰国警方坚决否认了酷刑指控。他们坚持认为审讯是按程序进行的，两名被告都是自愿认罪的。检察官表示，由于法医证据确凿，撤回供词不会对案件产生任何影响。汉娜·威瑟里奇和戴维·米勒的家人抨击了关于佐林和怀波被当作替罪羊的报道，并对调查表示信心。米勒一家说：“从我们所看到的来看，嫌疑人很难为自己辩护。针对他们的证据似乎强有力且令人信服。”

40
00:50:47.000 --> 00:52:09.000
For supporters of Zorlin and Waypo, the DNA evidence that supposedly linked them to the crime scene was also dubious. The authorities had never provided the detailed DNA test results which should include statistical data analysis and a probability ratio. Instead, they merely presented a one-page report that contained handwritten alterations to the dates and no stamp to confirm that the DNA had been tested in a laboratory that complied with internationally accepted standards. There was no documented chain of custody or case notes as would be required in any Western country. Furthermore, DNA testing is a complex process that can take a significant amount of time, but in Zorlin and Waypo's case, investigators were able to produce a result in around 24 hours. These discrepancies prompted accusations that the DNA evidence had either been planted or manipulated to frame the accused. Jane Torpen, an Australian expert on DNA profiling who looked at the evidence, said, Crime scenes are notoriously difficult to gather quality DNA samples from.
